   "title": "Figure 2.3.4 · WIMP: the four features of a GUI",
   "alt": "A simplified desktop screen with four labelled features. W, window: a rectangular area showing a document, with a title bar and minimise, maximise and close (X) buttons, which can be moved, resized and closed. I, icons: small pictures on the desktop for a folder, a document and a recycle bin. M, menu: a menu bar reading File, Edit, View, with the File menu pulled down to show New, Open, Save and Print. P, pointer: an arrow controlled by a mouse, touchpad or finger, resting on the Save command.",
   "caption": "Spell out \"graphical user interface\" and name at least two WIMP features with what they do. Writing only \"GUI\" may lose the definition mark.",
