  {
   "screen": "Transmission media 1: wired (guided) media",
   "title": "Figure 2.5.5 · Inside the three wired media",
   "alt": "Three rows, each with a labelled cross-section of a cable and its key facts. Twisted pair: an outer jacket around four pairs of copper wires, each pair twisted to reduce interference. Facts: electrical signals, about 100 metres per run; cheap and flexible, the standard LAN cable; unshielded (UTP) cable picks up electrical interference; used to connect PCs to a switch in a classroom. Coaxial cable: from the centre out, a copper core, insulation, a metal shield and an outer jacket. Facts: electrical signals; the metal shield gives better shielding and more bandwidth than basic twisted pair; used for cable TV and cable broadband. Fibre-optic cable: a glass core, cladding around it and a protective jacket. Facts: pulses of light in glass or plastic; very high bandwidth over long distances; immune to electrical interference and hard to tap; used for backbones and submarine cables.",
   "caption": "Twisted pair and coaxial cable carry electrical signals along copper; fibre carries pulses of light, which is why it is immune to electrical interference.",
   "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 640 380\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\"><defs><marker id=\"M2U5-5-a\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0L10,5L0,10z\" class=\"f-gold\"/></marker><marker id=\"M2U5-5-k\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0L10,5L0,10z\" class=\"f-ink\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"16\" y=\"12\" width=\"608\" height=\"112\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-none s-line\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"30\" y=\"34\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\"><tspan class=\"f-blue\">TWISTED PAIR</tspan></text><rect x=\"16\" y=\"134\" width=\"608\" height=\"112\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-none s-line\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"30\" y=\"156\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\"><tspan class=\"f-blue\">COAXIAL CABLE</tspan></text><rect x=\"16\" y=\"256\" width=\"608\" height=\"112\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-none s-line\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"30\" y=\"278\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\"><tspan class=\"f-blue\">FIBRE-OPTIC CABLE</tspan></text><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"80\" r=\"34\" class=\"f-softb s-muted\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"87.8\" cy=\"96.3\" r=\"6\" class=\"f-gold s-ink\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"96.3\" cy=\"87.8\" r=\"6\" class=\"f-gold s-ink\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"63.7\" cy=\"87.8\" r=\"6\" class=\"f-surface s-ink\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"72.2\" cy=\"96.3\" r=\"6\" class=\"f-surface s-ink\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"72.2\" cy=\"63.7\" r=\"6\" class=\"f-gold s-ink\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"63.7\" cy=\"72.2\" r=\"6\" class=\"f-gold s-ink\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"96.3\" cy=\"72.2\" r=\"6\" class=\"f-surface s-ink\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"87.8\" cy=\"63.7\" r=\"6\" class=\"f-surface s-ink\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"108\" y1=\"61\" x2=\"136\" y2=\"56\" class=\"s-ink\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"140\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"13\">outer jacket</text><line x1=\"98\" y1=\"92\" x2=\"136\" y2=\"92\" class=\"s-ink\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"140\" y=\"88\" font-size=\"13\">copper pairs, each</text><text x=\"140\" y=\"105\" font-size=\"13\">pair twisted</text><text x=\"330\" y=\"46\" font-size=\"13\"><tspan x=\"330\">Electrical signals; about 100 m per run</tspan><tspan x=\"330\" dy=\"18\">Cheap, flexible: the standard LAN cable</tspan><tspan x=\"330\" dy=\"18\">UTP picks up electrical interference</tspan><tspan x=\"330\" dy=\"18\">Use: PCs to a switch in a classroom</tspan></text><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"202\" r=\"34\" class=\"f-softb s-muted\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"202\" r=\"27\" class=\"f-none s-ink\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\"/><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"202\" r=\"22\" class=\"f-soft s-line\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"202\" r=\"7\" class=\"f-gold\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><line x1=\"97\" y1=\"173\" x2=\"136\" y2=\"166\" class=\"s-ink\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"140\" y=\"170\" font-size=\"13\">outer jacket</text><line x1=\"104\" y1=\"190\" x2=\"136\" y2=\"186\" class=\"s-ink\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"140\" y=\"190\" font-size=\"13\">metal shield</text><line x1=\"98\" y1=\"208\" x2=\"136\" y2=\"206\" class=\"s-ink\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"140\" y=\"210\" font-size=\"13\">insulation</text><line x1=\"85\" y1=\"205\" x2=\"136\" y2=\"226\" class=\"s-ink\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"140\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"13\">copper core</text><text x=\"330\" y=\"168\" font-size=\"13\"><tspan x=\"330\">Electrical signals</tspan><tspan x=\"330\" dy=\"18\">Metal shield: better shielding and more</tspan><tspan x=\"330\" dy=\"18\">bandwidth than basic twisted pair</tspan><tspan x=\"330\" dy=\"18\">Use: cable TV and cable broadband</tspan></text><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"324\" r=\"34\" class=\"f-softb s-muted\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"324\" r=\"20\" class=\"f-soft s-gold\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"324\" r=\"8\" class=\"f-gold\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><line x1=\"104\" y1=\"300\" x2=\"136\" y2=\"296\" class=\"s-ink\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"140\" y=\"300\" font-size=\"13\">protective jacket</text><line x1=\"98\" y1=\"318\" x2=\"136\" y2=\"318\" class=\"s-ink\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"140\" y=\"322\" font-size=\"13\">cladding</text><line x1=\"86\" y1=\"329\" x2=\"136\" y2=\"340\" class=\"s-ink\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"140\" y=\"344\" font-size=\"13\">glass core</text><text x=\"330\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"13\"><tspan x=\"330\">Pulses of light in glass or plastic</tspan><tspan x=\"330\" dy=\"18\">Very high bandwidth, long distances</tspan><tspan x=\"330\" dy=\"18\">Immune to electrical interference;</tspan><tspan x=\"330\" dy=\"18\">hard to tap. Use: submarine cables</tspan></text></svg>"
  }
