   "screen": "Hypertext and hyperlinks",
   "title": "Figure 2.9.4 · Reading in a line, or jumping by hyperlinks",
   "alt": "Left: the printed manual for a new car, drawn as six pages joined by arrows in a fixed order, page 1 to page 6. The author decides the order. Right: the same information as hypertext, five small topic documents (contents, warning lights, tyre pressure, air-conditioning and servicing) joined by green hyperlinks. One reader's path is highlighted in gold with numbered steps: contents, then tyre pressure, then warning lights, then air-conditioning. The reader, not the author, chooses the order and selection of topics.",
   "caption": "Hypertext is the non-linear way of organising information; a hyperlink is the clickable element that makes each jump.",
